[h1]Homesteader[/h1]
Grow it, put it by, live off the land. Tribal survival, farm-to-table crafting, wells and irrigation, cool storage, comforts, and off-grid power — for colonies far from the glitterworld supply chain.

[b]RimWorld 1.6.[/b] Requires [b]Harmony[/b]. Chinese Simplified and Russian included. Safe to add mid-save.
Do [b]not[/b] keep an old standalone Wellspring mod enabled (that content ships here; Wellspring_* defNames are preserved).

[h2]Tribal survival (no research)[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Drying rack[/b] — jerky, dried produce, fruit leather, dried mushrooms, and pemmican without needing pemmican research
[*] Field crops, basic storage crates, barrels, and pallets
[/list]

[h2]Primitive homestead[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Curing rack[/b] and [b]smokehouse[/b] for salted and smoked meat
[*] Hayloft and ingredient barrel for bulk farm storage
[*] Orchard trees (apple, cherry, sugar maple)
[/list]

[h2]Farmstead crafting[/h2]
[list]
[*] Grain mill, butter churn, cheese press, pickling crock, and homestead hearth
[*] Dairy pipeline: skim cream → churn butter (+ buttermilk) or press cheese; wax or smoke cheese
[*] Sugar, honey, or maple syrup for jam, porridge, and cider; butter for bread and flapjacks
[*] Pantry meals: toast and jam, ploughman's lunch, honey porridge, pumpkin pie, buttermilk biscuits
[*] Cider vinegar, vinegar pickles, apple cider, and homestead soap
[*] Favorite-food mood for every humanlike (Homesteader + vanilla pool); maypole harvest cheer
[/list]

[h2]Water & irrigation[/h2]
[list]
[*] Rain barrel (cheap trickle) → cistern (sheltered stockpile that also fills itself) → water tower (24 stacks, faster catch, critical haul)
[*] Hand-dug well (5 jugs on demand) → deep well (20 jugs a haul). Solar still is the arid sidegrade: boiled water without a stove
[*] Stone fountain drinks about two water jugs a day; courtyard beauty only counts while it is flowing
[*] Irrigated soil and irrigated planter (+30% fertility) after irrigation research
[*] Boiled water, mud bricks, and clean bandages crafted from water
[*] Optional [b]Dubs Bad Hygiene[/b]: rain barrel / cistern / water tower store plumbing water; hand-dug well is a primitive groundwater source; deep well is a piped deep inlet. Jug water for irrigation still works
[/list]

[h2]Orchard & apiary[/h2]
[list]
[*] Apple and cherry trees: slow-growing, regrowing orchard fruit for cider, jam, and eating fresh
[*] Sugar maple: tap for maple sap and boil it into maple syrup at the hearth — then griddle flapjacks
[*] Beehives produce beeswax alongside honey; render it into slow-burning beeswax candles
[/list]

[h2]Around the farmhouse[/h2]
[list]
[*] Preserves shelf: beautiful display storage for jams, pickles, cheese, dairy, honey, and syrup
[*] Nesting box: a snug straw-lined bed for small animals
[*] Harvest maypole: a ribboned gathering spot colonists celebrate around
[*] Polyarmory trait: polycule members (lovers and metamours with the trait) are fine sharing multi-person beds (works with Polyamory Beds)
[/list]

[h2]Livestock, fiber & pantry[/h2]
[list]
[*] Chicken coop (eggs); animal mash from barley, pumpkin, or hay
[*] Render lard/tallow and stuff sausage from cured meats and herbs
[*] Flax crop, spinning wheel, loom, and homestead quilts (quilted beds need a quilt)
[*] Compost heap → fertilizer → composted soil (+45% fertility)
[*] Icehouse (≤0°C) and springhouse (≤8°C) passive cold storage
[*] Canning kitchen (mason jars, canned stew/jam), cider press (apple juice → cider), wash tub (soap scrub)
[*] [b]Pantry tab[/b] — preserved kinds in cellar/shelf/crates, days of food, what's closest to spoiling, and a [b]What can I make[/b] page (can-make-now with add-bill, one ingredient short, or locked)
[*] Spoilage triage (on by default): eat and preserve the stack closest to turning first
[*] [b]Preserve crate[/b] — pack a mixed lot of jam, cheese, cider, and jerky for trade in one click (jam cauldron or canning kitchen); crates count estimated nutrition and mixed-lot variety on the pantry tab
[*] [b]Tastes tab[/b] — favorites and possible food allergies per humanlike; allergies stay hidden until first reaction; favorite meals give mood
[*] Seed saving: harvest drops saved seed; replant your stock and the line slowly takes to this soil
[/list]

[h2]Research & progression[/h2]
[list]
[*] Primitive homestead, food preservation, farmstead crafting, homestead storage, brewing, comforts, and advanced homestead
[*] Livestock, textiles, soil and cold storage, pantry craft
[*] Wellcraft → irrigation / waterworks
[*] Root cellar (passive cool storage ≤5°C), large storage crate, jam cauldron, and wood-burning generator
[*] Dedicated Homesteader research tab
[/list]

[h2]Scenario & storyteller[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Homesteaders[/b] — three settlers with livestock, seed, and hand tools; locks the Azrael storyteller
[*] [b]Azrael[/b] — Cassandra-style pacing with a bit more Misc / ThreatSmall for series flavor (Living World, Stormproof, homestead life). Canonical copy ships here; the optional Azrael showcase mod adds The Deep Homestead scenario
[/list]

[h2]Power[/h2]
Compact battery, battery bank, advanced battery, ultratech battery, portable chemfuel generator, and wood-burning generator.

[h2]Which station?[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Drying rack vs curing rack[/b] — drying rack needs no research (jerky, dried produce, fruit leather, dried mushrooms, pemmican). Curing rack unlocks with Primitive homestead and salts meat (and chips rock salt). Different jobs — not duplicates
[*] [b]Root cellar vs icehouse vs springhouse[/b] — root cellar is the large passive larder (≤5°C). Icehouse is colder and smaller (≤0°C). Springhouse is milder (≤8°C) for dairy and produce by the farmhouse
[*] [b]Homestead hearth vs wood stove[/b] — hearth cooks pantry meals. Wood stove only heats the room, off-grid — it does not cook
[/list]

[h2]Notes[/h2]
[list]
[*] Odyssey owners get salted and smoked fish recipes automatically
[*] Requires the Harmony mod (C# for root cellar cooling, pantry, tastes, and favorite foods)
[*] Safe to add to a save. Before removing it, deconstruct the mod's buildings and use up or sell its items
[*] Optional unique refresh art is [b]not[/b] in the Workshop download. Copy [b]Textures/HomesteaderRefresh[/b] from the GitHub repo into this mod folder, then Mod Options → Use refreshed textures (off by default). Original sprites always ship
[/list]

Pairs naturally with Stormproof (grid defense on Homesteader batteries and generators).
